# G4 acceptance gates — assets + inventory domains (2026-09-14)

## Commands

- cp -R hub src/pages/{assets,inventory} → crm src/pages/: 52 files, `diff -rq` byte-identical (pre route-fork)
- portal `pnpm tsc --noEmit` → EXIT=0
- `node --import tsx/esm examples/kb-agent/scripts/nocobase-portal-deploy.mts` ×2 →
  tree hash 4ba06b4ee3b7177708d9e04cf55ca41a71e3d01f both runs (identical)
- `node --import tsx/esm examples/kb-agent/scripts/nocobase-hub-modules.mts` ×2 →
  first run: hub_as_assets.tag/value added, 24-row backfill, hub_as_maintenance.vendor
  migrated belongsTo→input; second run: `already input (kept)`, `backfill 0 rows` (idempotent)

## Schema drift fixes (seed-side, G4-discovered)

- hub_as_assets lacked the portal list/sort column `tag` and the ledger value column
  `value` (default sorter ORDER BY tag made the list query 500). Both added via
  ensurePortalFields with a 24-row demo backfill (AST-1000…, US$ values).
- hub_as_maintenance.vendor was a belongsTo (vendor_id bigint) while the template form
  posts free text; NocoBase coerced the string into the bigint FK and 500'd. Migrated
  to an input column once, carrying provider names over (0 legacy rows referenced one).

## Route fork (recorded divergence from the frozen Hub source)

- crmRoutes.products ("/products", CRM price book) and inventoryRoutes.products
  collided; per the CRM-native-wins rule the inventory catalog nests under
  /inventory/products (4 constants in pages/inventory/routes.ts). All other
  assets/inventory routes are collision-free and byte-identical to Hub.

